{; Unit: queued compute submissions.
 ; Provenance: core.async.flow alpha3 uses a fixed buffer of 10 per channel;
 ; the scheduling testbed preserved it because a full channel parks the
 ; submitter and loses no work.
 :seon.config.flow.compute/queue-depth 10

 ; :seon.config.flow.compute/concurrency is deliberately ABSENT here:
 ; its default is COMPUTED at (seon.config/defaults) — the machine's
 ; available processors — because a shipped literal is only ever right
 ; on the machine that shipped it. A manifest may override with an
 ; explicit integer. (Calibration context: 2026-07-25 measured 18 cores
 ; here; 22 concurrent evals queued 4 with 71 ms max wait.)

 ; The eval result caps: how much of an agent value `seon.sci.admit`
 ; projects into a receipt's result-edn. Units below; provenance: the
 ; 2026-07-27 admission probes (tmp/n3-admission-probe/) — a naive
 ; recursive walk dies at ~5000 depth and pr-str at ~20000, so the node
 ; budget is the real bound and depth/width merely shape it.
 ; Unit: nesting levels.
 :seon.config.eval.result/max-depth 12
 ; Unit: elements retained per collection.
 :seon.config.eval.result/max-collection 64
 ; Unit: characters retained per string.
 :seon.config.eval.result/max-string 4096
 ; Unit: total nodes visited across the whole projection.
 :seon.config.eval.result/max-nodes 4096

 ; Unit: milliseconds of wall clock per agent evaluation.
 ; Provenance: the ONLY limit sci has — it counts no steps, so this is
 ; the whole bound on an interpreted form (reference-code/sci/doc/
 ; interrupt.md:23-35). Calibrated against the measured shapes rather
 ; than a feeling: an authored infinite loop dies at ~55 ms once the
 ; flag flips, and the suite's runaway cases stop inside 300 ms, so a
 ; 30 s ceiling is three orders of magnitude above the mechanism's
 ; latency and still bounded well below a human's patience. It bounds
 ; INTERPRETED work only: a form blocked inside a host call never
 ; enters an interpreted body and is covered by the caller's submission
 ; backstop and the process boundary, never by this.
 :seon.config.eval/time-limit-ms 30000

 ; Unit: count of same-signature faults since this process started.
 ; Provenance: the second escalation condition (the first is "no
 ; attributable agent"). Three says a fault that happened once was
 ; noise, twice was bad luck, and three times is a pattern the
 ; escalation owner must hear about. Counted by query over committed
 ; facts; there is no stored tally to drift.
 :seon.config.error/recurrence-limit 3

 ; Unit: agent-to-agent hops in ONE causal chain, counted back through
 ; committed transaction metadata to the last message that came from
 ; outside the agent population.
 ; Provenance: the quarry shipped 8 (`seon.warn/hop-cap`,
 ; src-old/seon/agent/message.cljc:316) and its scar is recorded — a
 ; GLOBAL newest-inbound count summed every wake-chain hop, so a routine
 ; two-round delegation (parent→A→parent→B→parent) hit the cap and
 ; silently deadlocked, and the fix was a per-peer count with a
 ; human-message barrier. This chain walk is that fix arrived at
 ; structurally instead: the barrier is free, because a message from
 ; outside the population has no triggering transaction to walk back
 ; through and therefore starts at zero by construction. 16 is that
 ; hard-won 8 doubled, on the reasoning that the quarry's number was
 ; calibrated against a count that OVERSTATED depth: eight rounds of
 ; unattended ping-pong is a runaway, four is a conversation, and the
 ; cost of being wrong low is a delegation that dies mid-thought.
 :seon.config.message/max-chain 16

 ; WHO hears what nobody else can be told about. It names the root agent
 ; because boot now SEEDS one — the reason this was absent when the dial
 ; landed was that a default naming an agent that may not exist would be
 ; a lie, and that is no longer the case: every cluster has a root from
 ; its first transaction, free, with no process and no tokens.
 ; The dial stays OPTIONAL in the shape, and that is not vestigial —
 ; a manifest may override it to absent, and absence still means the
 ; error fact is committed with no escalation message. `commit-tx` also
 ; refuses to address an agent this cluster does not have, so a dial
 ; pointing at a typo costs the message, never the record.
 :seon.config.error/escalate-to "root"

 ; Unit: categorical core-fault disposition.
 ; Provenance: the 2026-07-27 error ruling requires development to fail
 ; loudly and production to degrade only by explicit configuration.
 :seon.config/on-core-error :panic

 ; THE VIEW'S PORT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and absence is the state: with
 ; no dial the port is DERIVED from the cluster name (7700-7999, FNV-1a
 ; over the name — `seon.render.web/derived-port`), so every named
 ; cluster is bookmarkable and answers on the same port after every
 ; restart. Setting this pins one instead, and an explicit port is
 ; somebody's decision that outranks a derivation.
 ; Unit: TCP port. A derived port that is already taken falls back to an
 ; ephemeral one and reports BOTH numbers.

 ; Unit: milliseconds between repaints of one tab. Provenance: 16 ms is
 ; one frame at 60 fps, the owner's stated bar, and it is a FLOOR rather
 ; than a tick — a burst of commits inside one window costs one repaint
 ; and a quiet cluster costs none.
 :seon.config.render/coalesce-ms 16

 ; THE MODEL SEAM. DeepSeek is the standing default provider; the loop
 ; is installed at boot, so the provider it would call has to be a fact
 ; rather than a literal in a drive script. Nothing here spends
 ; anything: an installed loop with no trigger makes no call.
 ; Unit: absolute URL of one OpenAI-compatible completions endpoint.
 :seon.config.ai/endpoint "https://api.deepseek.com/chat/completions"

 ; Unit: the provider's own model name.
 :seon.config.ai/model "deepseek-chat"

 ; Unit: the NAME of an environment variable. Never the credential —
 ; the key is read at the leaf, never becomes a datom, never enters Git.
 :seon.config.ai/api-key-variable "DEEPSEEK_API_KEY"

 ; Unit: milliseconds. Provenance: the live drives measured a real plan
 ; reply at 2.7 s; sixty seconds is the deadline on an unobservable
 ; remote call, not a target.
 :seon.config.ai/timeout-ms 60000

 ; THE BACKUP DESCRIPTOR ROW IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. A shipped backup
 ; would be a second provider this repository picked for everybody, and
 ; the honest default is "one target, no failover": with no
 ; :seon.config.ai.backup/model, `disposition` never returns
 ; :failover-now and the no-backup path below is the only resilience
 ; there is. A cluster that wants failover sets ONE dial when the backup
 ; is another model at the same provider, or three more when it is not.
 ; Absence is the state; there is no nil to read.

 ; THE BACKOFF STRATEGY, and it runs on exactly one path: a
 ; conclusively UNPAID transient failure with no backup configured.
 ; Nothing here can re-call a transmitted request — `seon.ai/disposition`
 ; returns :backoff for exactly three error classes, and a request that
 ; may have cost money is not one of them.
 ;
 ; Unit: milliseconds before the first retry.
 ; Provenance: DeepSeek's live plan replies measured 2.7 s, so a first
 ; wait shorter than a second would re-ask a busy provider inside its
 ; own service time; 500 ms is half of that floor and the smallest wait
 ; that is not effectively "immediately".
 :seon.config.ai.retry/base-delay-ms 500

 ; Unit: dimensionless growth factor per retry.
 ; Provenance: doubling is the standard exponential backoff shape and is
 ; what `again`'s multiplicative-strategy composes; anything gentler
 ; makes the retry count the bound instead of the wait.
 :seon.config.ai.retry/multiplier 2.0

 ; Unit: fraction of each delay applied as random spread.
 ; Provenance: jitter exists so N clusters retrying one outage do not
 ; re-synchronize; a quarter of the delay decorrelates them without
 ; making the schedule unrecognizable to somebody reading the log.
 :seon.config.ai.retry/jitter-fraction 0.25

 ; Unit: milliseconds; the cap on any single wait.
 :seon.config.ai.retry/maximum-delay-ms 4000

 ; Unit: count of retries after the first attempt.
 ; Provenance: a rate limit or a 503 either clears in seconds or is an
 ; outage; two retries distinguishes those two cases and a third only
 ; delays telling the agent.
 :seon.config.ai.retry/maximum-retries 2

 ; Unit: milliseconds of TOTAL waiting across all retries.
 ; Provenance: THE BINDING BOUND, and it is bound by the run lease, not
 ; by patience. A turn holds its run under a 60 s lease and the model
 ; call itself may take the full 60 s deadline, so the waiting budget
 ; has to be small enough that a backed-off turn does not routinely
 ; outlive its own claim. Three seconds is under 5% of the lease and
 ; still covers the base + one doubled wait.
 :seon.config.ai.retry/maximum-total-delay-ms 3000}
